  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Umoyo Wathu Health Systems Strengthening, Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an 3,5 year programme supported by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office and undertaken in collaboration with University College London and the Global Health Informatics Institute (GHII) in Malawi. The purpose of this programme is to build quality improvement networks between primary health facilities and hospitals and expand use of Neotree&apos;s digital health platform to 11 additional sites (1 district hospital, 10 primary healthcare facilities). Neotree will use programme activities and outputs to deliver a business case/ plan for larger scale-up of Neotree across Malawi. This will involve work to improve the functionality of Neotree based on experience from a pilot of its system in primary care and evaluating the impact of implementing Neotree across this network of health facilities in Malawi on (i) quality of care and (ii) outcomes for sick and vulnerable newborns and (iii) the effectiveness of the implementation strategy across the network. This will also involve capacity building work in academic experience of digital health implementation and evaluation (which includes an academic partnership with the implementation science team at Kamuzu University of Health Sciences (KUHeS). Throughout this project, Neotree will facilitate shared South to South learning, dissemination to key stakeholders and capacity building.</narrative>
  </description>
